  "summary": "A person stands in the rain at night, upright, meeting your eyes. In their chest is a real window \u2014 a lamp, two cups, a plant, someone at home \u2014 and the same light is caught in their eyes. Down the street, every other person carries a small lit window too.\n\nThe words are the part you can take with you: someone is home in there. Leave them warmer than you found them. You are in there too. Before the harsh word, the turned back, the raised hand.\n\nThe still is `output/someone-is-home.svg`. The film, `output/someone-is-home.mp4`, is the act of looking: a dim stranger, then the room, then the whole street, then the words."
